#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:299
msgid "When the visitor asks what something would cost, or how much of something they would need, work out an estimate instead of refusing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:300
msgid "Every price, rate and fee must come from the excerpts. Never invent one, and never adjust one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:301
msgid "For anything the excerpts cannot tell you — how much people consume, how many working days a month has — use the ASSUMPTIONS below."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:302
msgid "Do every calculation with the calculate tool. Never work arithmetic out yourself, even when it looks easy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:303
msgid "Write the estimate in this order: the assumptions you used, then what the numbers work out to, then the rounded total. Say which figures came from the site and which are assumptions."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:304
msgid "Call it an estimate, and invite the visitor to ask for an exact quote."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:305
msgid "If a price you need is not in the excerpts, say exactly which figure is missing and offer to put them in touch, rather than guessing at it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wp-ai-advisor-openai-client.php:306
msgid "An estimate built from excerpt prices plus the assumptions below is grounded: set \"grounded\" to true."
msgstr ""

